  "scope": "Positive parallel transport fixes the semidirect-product action. Nested inclusions and restricted retractions give inverse fundamental-group maps, and the meridian normal closure gives the exact tube presentation. Projection gives Z/m; (v,c) maps to v-c lambda/m with the displayed inverse, proving the rational rank. Normalization spheres joined by stars map to the conductor by contractible-star collapse, and sphere collapse induces the incidence-graph fundamental-group isomorphism. The tree edge count gives e(C)=c+1 and the stated e(S)>=3. Universal Laurent coefficient convolution verifies the matrix identities, complete determinant expansions verify the sign, and formal cell counts agree. The stronger intermediate value stays only in the check record. The held adjacent gap remains unchanged and root-owned. All18 Programs rows remain and one is appended.",
